<title>FINLAND: Metsa-Serla Q1 profit falls 46 pct.</title>
<headline>Metsa-Serla Q1 profit falls 46 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to end-March-</p>
<p>					(million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after financial item		    129 vs 239</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   0.22 vs 1.15</p>
<p> Net sales					  3,934 vs 3,757</p>
<p> Operating profit				   288 vs 393</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' median forecast for Metsa-Serla's Q1 profit before extraordinary items had been 20 million markka (range 50 million markka loss to 170 million markka profit).  </p>
<p> Depreciation					 310 vs 269</p>
<p> Net exchange gains, losses	     charge 22 vs 26 charge</p>
<p> Other financial expenses		charge 137 vs 128 charge</p>
<p> Extraordinary income				32 vs nil</p>
<p> Extraordinary expenses			     1 vs 13</p>
<p> Profit before minorities, taxes		160 vs 226</p>
<p> Taxes						  102 vs 54</p>
<p> Minorities				    charge 6 vs 36 charge</p>
<p> Net profit					    52 vs 136</p>
<p> Equity to assets ratio (percent)	    32.6 vs 36.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Finnish forest industry group is Metsa-Serla Oy. @</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 80 6805 0245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
